# Port patch for retail data: The Mercenaries room r402 (the waterworld) sets its enemies as the retail st4_0.rel
# does (US, EU, JP read with retail_code.py on 31.10.2026; the JP code is the EU code). The retail list
# etc/omake01.esl has three new entries for r402 (0xE3, 0xE7, 0xEB; US, EU and JP alike, EU/JP also make 0xAB/0xAC
# hide and jump), and the room code changed with it:
# - R402EmSetMain: the order of the areas changed, the boat events (area 0x4000000) start with up to 8 active
#   enemies instead of 6, a new wave in area 0x2000 (entries 0xE3 / 0xE7 / 0xEB, up to 15) takes slots 0x5A..0x5C,
#   the later slots moved (0x72 slots instead of 0x70; door event 01 uses 0x5D..0x5F, door event 02 0x65..0x6B).
# - R402Init: the six starting enemies 0xA2..0xA7 search for the player instead of walking to him.
# - em_destroy (every 300 frames): the retail releases keep inactive enemies that are still on their way.
# - R402EmSetSub: goto mode 15 (patch 0165) instead of 0xC, and the list entry is recorded in the enemy
#   (emset_no; EmSetEvent leaves 0xFF): EU and JP only, the US release keeps 0xC and 0xFF.
# Debug discs unchanged (the prototype's list has no entries 0xE3 / 0xE7 / 0xEB).
